Chapter: ElasticBloom

  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter MathLib
  cites Foreword chapter BloomFilter
  cites Foreword chapter ElasticHash

 A hash map combining a Bloom filter negative-path accelerator with an
 elastic hash table. The Bloom filter gates every lookup: if it reports
 absent, the multi-level probe is skipped entirely, turning the miss
 path from O(num-levels) hash computations into k bit checks.

 Insertions write to both structures. Lookups check the Bloom filter
 first, then fall through to the elastic table only on a probable hit.
 False positives from the Bloom filter cost one elastic probe sequence;
 false negatives never occur, so a Bloom "no" is authoritative.

 An ElasticBloomMap is a record containing:
   filter -- Bloom filter for fast negative answers.
   table  -- ElasticTable backing store.

 To eb-new gives ElasticBloomMap, creating an empty map sized for the
 given expected entry count. The Bloom filter is sized at 10 bits per
 expected entry with 7 hash functions (~0.8% false positive rate).

 To eb-get gives Maybe a, checking the Bloom filter first. Returns None
 immediately when the filter reports absent.

 To eb-put gives ElasticBloomMap, inserting into both the filter and the
 table.

 To eb-has gives Boolean, True when the key is probably present. This is
 the fast path: Bloom-only, no table probe. False positives are possible.

 To eb-has-exact gives Boolean, True when the key is definitely present.
 Checks the Bloom filter, then confirms in the table.

 To eb-size gives Integer, the number of entries inserted.

 To eb-capacity gives Integer, the total slot count of the backing table.

 We say:

Section: Types

  ElasticBloomMap a = record {
    filter : BloomFilter,
    table : ElasticTable a
  }

Section: Construction

  eb-new : Integer -> ElasticBloomMap a
  eb-new (expected) =
    let safe = if expected < 8 then 8 else expected
    in let bloom-bits = math-min 65535 (safe * 10)
    in ElasticBloomMap {
      filter = bloom-new bloom-bits 7,
      table = elastic-new safe
    }

Section: Lookup

  eb-get : ElasticBloomMap a, Text -> Maybe a
  eb-get (m) (key) =
    if bloom-contains-text (m.filter) key
      then elastic-get (m.table) key
      else None

  eb-has : ElasticBloomMap a, Text -> Boolean
  eb-has (m) (key) =
    bloom-contains-text (m.filter) key

  eb-has-exact : ElasticBloomMap a, Text -> Boolean
  eb-has-exact (m) (key) =
    if bloom-contains-text (m.filter) key
      then elastic-has (m.table) key
      else False

Section: Insert

  eb-put : ElasticBloomMap a, Text, a -> ElasticBloomMap a
  eb-put (m) (key) (value) =
    ElasticBloomMap {
      filter = bloom-add-text (m.filter) key,
      table = elastic-put (m.table) key value
    }

Section: Queries

  eb-size : ElasticBloomMap a -> Integer
  eb-size (m) = elastic-size (m.table)

  eb-capacity : ElasticBloomMap a -> Integer
  eb-capacity (m) = elastic-capacity (m.table)

